VERSION ""

CM_ "BMW F/G Series PT-CAN (500 kbit/s) — RaceChrono community CSV + G29/J29 map (thesecretingredient.neocities.org/bmw/can/g29/).";
CM_ "Signals marked unconfirmed in the source CSV are included only when bit layout was specified; scaling follows RaceChrono formulas where they differ from CSV byte columns.";
CM_ "0x0D9 pedal/throttle: start bits follow RaceChrono bitsToUintLe (16, 12) and (32, 12), not the CSV start-byte columns.";
CM_ "0x254 wheel speeds: G29 uses km/h with factor 1/64 (same as 0.015625); CSV label 'rad/s' is treated as km/h here.";
CM_ "0x330 on PT-CAN is fuel (used / lamp / range). Same ID 0x330 on E-series K-CAN is odometer — do not mix buses.";
CM_ "——— K-CAN / body bus (100 kbit/s) — OEM TPMS is not on PT-CAN for F/G (forum: RDC via DSC/FEM, not seen on PT-CAN sniffs).";
CM_ "K-CAN TPMS IDs below are E-series references (MorGuux KCAN notes, nberlette E90 DBC): 0x2B2 wheel pressures, 0x31C RDC status, 0x31D puncture status.";
CM_ "Byte layout for 0x2B2 is UNVERIFIED on F/G — guessed 8-bit * 0.025 bar per corner (McLaren-style). Capture K-CAN on your car before trusting.";
CM_ "Oil pressure: no public CAN decode found for F/G PT-CAN; use OBD2/UDS (e.g. genericDiag) instead.";

